{{Politics of Okaiken}}

The {{Nihongo|'''Ikazaki Cabinet'''|五十崎内閣|Ikazaki Naikaku}}, officially designated the 110th Cabinet of Okaiken, is the executive government of Okaiken established on 20 May 2026 following the [[Okaiken general election, 2026|May 2026 general election]]. The administration is formed from a tripartite left-of-centre parliamentary coalition between the [[Sanese Communist Party]] (SCP), the [[Okaiken Socialist Party]] (OSP), and the [[Social Democratic Party (Okaiken)|Social Democratic Party]] (SDP), augmented by the confidence and supply support of independent representative [[Hayashi Akihiro]] of the [[Ogasawara Subprefecture|Ogasawara]] third district. The governing coalition commands 251 seats in the 475-member [[House of Commoners of Okaiken]], providing a thirteen-seat absolute parliamentary majority.

The executive is led by Prime Minister [[Kousuke Ikazaki]] of the SCP, a former Defence Minister noted for ruthless administrative discipline, alongside Deputy Prime Minister [[Rento Nakayama]] of the OSP, who simultaneously leads the newly consolidated super-ministry portfolio of Social Affairs. The administration is historic as the first government in Sanese history to operate under the binding Yoshida Threshold, a constitutional coalition stipulation requiring that at least 40 percent of all cabinet portfolios be occupied by women. The cabinet assumed office in the aftermath of the collapse of the [[Honda-Nakayama Cabinet]], brought down by popular outrage following the [[Nakayama Station dragging incident]] and the structural collapse of automated infrastructure during the [[Satori AI Blackout Crisis]].

==Formation and coalition negotiations==

{{main|Okaiken general election, 2026}}

The collapse of the conservative-reformist Honda-Nakayama administration precipitated a snap election in early May 2026. The electorate delivered a severe rebuke to both the [[Progressive Party of Okaiken]] (PPO) and the [[Liberal Democratic Party (Okaiken)|Liberal Democratic Party]] (LDP). In the revised chamber, the SCP captured 115 seats, the OSP secured 100 seats, and the SDP surged to 36 seats, opening the path for an historic left-wing majority.

Coalition negotiations spanned seventy-two hours in an episode dubbed the Three-Day War by political commentators. Ideological friction centred on the SCP's demand for a centralized fortress state focused on corporate criminal liability and state capacity versus the OSP's emphasis on immediate social welfare redistribution and labor protection. SDP leader [[Shimane Yoshida]] entered the talks on the second day, leveraging her thirty-six votes to extract two non-negotiable guarantees: the codification of the Yoshida Threshold and the creation of dedicated cabinet posts for Gender Equality and Digital Sovereignty. A conclusive pact was finalized in an early-morning bilateral conference between Ikazaki and Nakayama on 19 May 2026, leading to the formal imperial investiture of the Cabinet at the Imperial Palace on 20 May 2026.

==Cabinet composition==

The cabinet consists of seventeen ministers of state, spanning nine representatives from the Sanese Communist Party, six from the Okaiken Socialist Party, and two from the Social Democratic Party.

